  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two reactions, involved in the commercial production of dihydrogen <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced></math>. The two reactions are carried out at temperature &ldquo;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&rdquo; and &ldquo;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&rdquo;, respectively</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mover><mi>CO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Catalyst</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>The temperatures <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are correctly related as</p>",
